+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdP4ex2LRnGxrPwLWZX5N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The constraint-based event scheduler is implemented, tested, and verified.\n\n## What was built\n\n**`src/scheduler.ts`** — the full implementation, re-exported through **`src/index.ts`** with all three API surfaces (named `schedule`, default export, and `Scheduler` class / `createScheduler` factory).\n\nThe algorithm works in three layers:\n\n1. **Cycle detection** — DFS over the prerequisite graph throws on any cycle, including self-references, before scheduling starts.\n2. **Greedy placement engine** — Kahn's topological processing places each event at its earliest feasible slot, enforcing capacity, the time window, per-room gaps, and prerequisite-end + gap ordering. Preferred rooms are honored whenever the event fits there at all (with a fallback mode that treats preference as a tiebreak only).\n3. **Portfolio search** — because a single greedy pass can't maximize the scheduled count, the engine runs ~28 orderings and keeps the best result: seven fixed heuristics (critical-path length, fewest-eligible-rooms first, attendees desc, duration asc/desc, input order), one *dynamic* ordering that re-sorts by each event's current earliest feasible start as rooms fill up, and 20 seeded random restarts — all crossed with the two preference modes. Results are compared by events scheduled, then preferences honored.\n\n**`tests/scheduler.test.ts`** — 20 tests covering every rule (capacity, window, default/custom/zero gap, prerequisites in any input order, cycles and self-references throwing, preferred-room honor and fallback, maximization, dependents of unschedulable events, and the export surface). Per the delegation setup, I wrote the exact test specifications and had the light worker transcribe the file; I verified its output by review and by running it.\n\n## Verification beyond the unit tests\n\n- **Property check**: 500 random instances, zero violations of any constraint (capacity, window, room gaps, prerequisite ordering, assignment/unscheduled partition).\n- **Optimality check**: compared against a brute-force optimum on 3×300 small random instances across three different seed sets — the scheduler matches the optimum in all 900. This process actually caught three real suboptimal cases mid-development, which drove the dynamic ordering and random-restart additions.\n- **Performance**: 300 events across 12 rooms schedules in ~75ms.\n\n`npm test` (20/20), `npm run build`, and `npm run lint` all pass clean."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":71237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2151efc-6b31-494a-8238-e56cb5a93fd1","uuid":"b7af78bd-aa57-4d4f-81f5-3a99e4b5c3a7","request_id":"req_011CdP4etffx5bcwfxm85wUN"}
